**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests`

**How to implement.** A setup as Domain data: an ordered optical path of slots, each slot one element of the table holding an item or nothing, and the revisions an experiment can reference (001 §J; the S8.2 brief: `Setup { name : SetupName; revision; slots }`, each slot holding an item (`ItemId`) or nothing plus its position on the beam and R1 / R2 / R3, or a dial reading; 'Experiments keep their captured-snapshot meaning through the setup revision: editing a setup that an experiment uses mints the next revision'; .spec-md §5, §6 'Version rule'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs`: `module Setups` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `BeamLayout.fs`, because a slot sits on a `BeamLayout.BeamHost`: one `<Compile Include="Setups.fs" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines: the setup, an ordered optical path of slots that the table draws (spec 0050 S8.2). It opens `Placement`, `Kit`, `ItemModels`, `Lifecycle` and `LibraryEntryFiles`; each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (2) `SlotTurn` = `PlacementTurn` (the slot's R1 is its placement's own) | `DialTurn of reading : Angle` (the slot's item turns on a dial set to this raw reading, and its R1 is the item's `DialSign.physicalAngleOf` of it, step 255). `SlotContent` = `EmptySlotContent` | `ItemInSlot of item : ItemId * turn : SlotTurn`, with `member this.itemOpt : ItemId option`. (3) `SetupSlot = { id : Library.ElementId; placement : ElementPlacement; zoom : BeamLayout.ElementZoom; beam : BeamLayout.BeamHost; content : SlotContent }`, one slot of a setup and the one table element that draws it: its stable id (an experiment's varied element names it), its placement (the catalogue kind, the position along its beam, R1 / R2 / R3, the locks, the emission and the library entry it is bound to, `Placement.fs:ElementPlacement`), its draw zoom, the beam it sits on and its content. It carries what `Experiments.ElementDescriptor` (`Experiments.fs:ElementDescriptor`) and `Scene.SceneElement` (`Scene.fs:SceneElement`) carry today, which steps 260 and 261 delete. `member this.layoutElement : BeamLayout.LayoutElement` is `{ id = this.id; placement = this.placement; host = this.beam; zoom = this.zoom }` (`BeamLayout.fs:LayoutElement`), what the one ray law lays out (AGENTS.md 'One ray law'). (4) `SetupRevisionRecord = { revision : SetupRevision; slots : SetupSlot list }`, an earlier revision kept for the experiments that reference it. (5) `Setup = { name : SetupName; revision : SetupRevision; slots : SetupSlot list; history : SetupRevisionRecord list }`: the slots in the table's order (the light source, the ray root, first), and the earlier revisions oldest first, as an item file keeps its history (step 215). The brief's three fields gain `history` because an experiment that references an earlier revision must still resolve its slots. Members: `this.reference : SetupReference` (its name and current revision); `this.slotsAt (revision : SetupRevision) : Result<SetupSlot list, SetupError>`, the current slots at the current revision, a history record's at an earlier one, and `UnknownSetupRevisionErr` naming the reference's `describe` otherwise; `this.heldItems : ItemId list`, the items the current slots and then each history record's slots hold, each once, in that order; `static member create (name : SetupName) (slots : SetupSlot list) (held : Setup list) : Result<Setup, SetupError>`, `DuplicateSetupNameErr` naming both names when a held setup's `name.fileStem` equals the name's ignoring case (every `<name>.setup-json` shares the kit root on Windows, step 216's rule for items) and otherwise the setup at `SetupRevision.first` with no history: CreateSetup's pure half (001 §P); and `this.revisedWith (slots : SetupSlot list) (pin : PinState) : Setup`, the setup after the table's slots are written over it, decided by `Lifecycle.decideVersioning` (`Lifecycle.fs:decideVersioning`, the one version rule) over `{ physics = this.slots; metadata = () }` and `{ physics = slots; metadata = () }` with `pin` (step 65's `PinState`): `KeepCurrent` answers the setup unchanged, `MutateInPlace` the setup holding `slots`, and `MintNextVersion` the setup at `revision.next` holding `slots`, its current revision and slots appended to `history`. A setup has no metadata beyond its name, so its slots alone decide. No cache, wire tag or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs`, `module SetupTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. Its fixture slots are test-local records over `ElementPlacement.create` (`Placement.fs`), zoom `BeamLayout.ElementZoom 5.0` and `BeamLayout.OnMainBeam`: `src` (`LightSource` at `RayModel.defaultSourcePoint`), `lp` (`LinearPolarizer` at x = −0.3 m) and `det` (`Detector` at `RayModel.defaultDetectorPoint`), each `EmptySlotContent`, and a test-local `ItemId`. `a slot lays out as the element it is, on its own beam, and names the item it holds`: `lp.layoutElement` holds `lp`'s id, placement, beam as `host` and zoom; `itemOpt` of `ItemInSlot (item, PlacementTurn)` is `Some item` and of `EmptySlotContent` `None`. `a setup answers its slots at its own revision and at each earlier one, and refuses a revision it never had`: a setup `Bench` at revision 3 with history records r1 and r2 of distinct slot lists answers each list at its revision, and revision 4 answers `UnknownSetupRevisionErr` whose reason names `'Bench' revision 4`. `a setup lists each item its revisions hold once, in order`: a setup whose current slots hold items A then B and whose history holds B then C lists A, B, C. `a setup is created at its first revision, and a name whose file the kit holds is refused`: `create (SetupName "Bench")` over no held setup is revision 1 with no history; over a held `bench` it answers `DuplicateSetupNameErr`, and `Bench: A` over a held `Bench_ A` too. `a setup's slots change in place until an experiment pins its revision, which then mints the next`: revising with equal slots answers the setup unchanged, pinned or not; with `lp` turned to R1 30° and `VersionUnpinned` the revision and history are unchanged and the slots are the new ones; with `VersionPinned` the setup is at revision 2 with the new slots and one history record holding revision 1 and the old slots; a second pinned change gives revision 3 with history r1 then r2.

**Acceptance.** After the setup shape lands, `Setups.fs` MUST hold `SlotTurn`, `SlotContent`, `SetupSlot`, `SetupRevisionRecord` and `Setup`, a setup MUST answer its slots at each revision it holds and refuse others, and `revisedWith` MUST mint the next revision exactly when the revision is pinned and the slots change; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot lays out as the element it is, on its own beam, and names the item it holds`, `a setup answers its slots at its own revision and at each earlier one, and refuses a revision it never had`, `a setup lists each item its revisions hold once, in order`, `a setup is created at its first revision, and a name whose file the kit holds is refused` and `a setup's slots change in place until an experiment pins its revision, which then mints the next`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
